  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Suppose $f:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ satisfies $f(x)\\le x$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and $f(x+y)\\le f(x)+f(y)$ for all $x,y\\in\\mathbb{R}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p34-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $f(0)=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(0)=0$, since $f(0)\\le0$ and $f(0)\\le2f(0)$ gives $f(0)\\ge0$.",
          "worked": "The first condition at $x=0$ gives $f(0)\\le0$. The second condition at $x=y=0$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}f(0)&\\le f(0)+f(0)\\\\f(0)&\\ge0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $0\\le f(0)\\le0$, so $f(0)=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, show that $f(x)=x$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p34-q16-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(x)=x\\quad\\text{for all }x\\in\\mathbb{R}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p34-q16-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use opposite inputs to obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(x)\\ge-f(-x)\\ge x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then combine with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f(x)\\le x",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For any $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$, part (a) and the second condition give\n$$0=f(0)=f(x+(-x))\\le f(x)+f(-x).$$\nThe first condition gives $f(-x)\\le-x$. Therefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&\\ge-f(-x)\\\\f(x)&\\ge x.\\end{align*}$$\nAlso $f(x)\\le x$ by the first condition. Hence $f(x)=x$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
